# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI Enablement Dashboard — CAP OData V4 Test Suite
# Run with: VS Code REST Client extension
# Server  : cds watch (local, mocked auth)
# Every request now needs a login. The job endpoints (/J4C) need admin; the screens' endpoints
# (/dashboard) need viewer or admin. Section E checks the role rules and the masking.
#
# Services
#   DashboardService  /dashboard   read side, used by the screens
#   J4CService        /J4C         jobs for the J4C initiative (SCIM sync, usage sync)
#
# Auth    : mocked users defined in .cdsrc.json
#           admin / admin   → DashboardAdmin and DashboardUserDetail (sees real names and emails)
#           viewer / viewer → DashboardViewer only (sees masked names and emails)
#
# Expected values below assume the sample CSVs (one-off test data, not real people):
#   Person.csv           15 persons (J4C has 13: 11 active, 2 inactive)
#   ActiveUserList.csv   164 roster rows
# Do NOT run the SCIM sync (section C) on top of those test CSVs: the test users
# are not in the real IAS group, so the sync would deactivate them. Use the CSVs
# for UI testing, or the sync for real data, not both.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@host       = http://localhost:4004
@baseUrl    = {{host}}/dashboard
@jobUrl     = {{host}}/J4C
@adminAuth  = Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4=
@viewerAuth = Basic dmlld2VyOnZpZXdlcg==

# YWRtaW46YWRtaW4=  = base64("admin:admin")
# dmlld2VyOnZpZXdlcg== = base64("viewer:viewer")

@initiativeId1 = 10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@initiativeId2 = 10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@initiativeId3 = 10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003
@scimId        = scim-usr-0015


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# A. INITIATIVES AND ENABLED USERS (Screen 1 and the Screen 2 header)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# 1. READ ALL INITIATIVES
# Expected: 200 OK, 3 initiatives, enabledUsers and statusCriticality filled in
### Read all initiatives
GET {{baseUrl}}/Initiatives
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 2. READ SINGLE INITIATIVE
# Expected: 200 OK, one row (J4C)
### Read single initiative (J4C)
GET {{baseUrl}}/Initiatives({{initiativeId1}})
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}


# 3. CREATE INITIATIVE
# Expected: 405 Method Not Allowed. Initiatives are read-only in this service (they come
#           from the seed data), so even an admin cannot create one here.
### Create new initiative, even admin gets 405
POST {{baseUrl}}/Initiatives
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name"      : "AI Code Review Pilot",
  "owner"     : "Platform Engineering Lead",
  "status"    : "ComingSoon",
  "launchDate": "2027-01-15",
  "iasGroup"  : "SAP_AI_CODE_REVIEW_ENDUSER"
}


# 4. CREATE INITIATIVE AS VIEWER
# Expected: 403 or 405. The service is read-only for everybody, so no role can create here.
### Create initiative as viewer — expect 403/405
POST {{baseUrl}}/Initiatives
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name"      : "Unauthorized Initiative",
  "owner"     : "Nobody",
  "status"    : "Live",
  "launchDate": "2026-10-01",
  "iasGroup"  : "SAP_UNAUTHORIZED_GROUP"
}


# 5. ENABLED USER COUNT
# Expected: 200 OK, { count: 11 } for J4C (if the helper counts active persons)
### Get enabled user count for J4C
GET {{baseUrl}}/getEnabledUserCount(initiativeId={{initiativeId1}})
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 6. ENABLED USER COUNT, initiative with no active users
# Expected: 200 OK, { count: 0 }
### Get enabled user count for initiative 3
GET {{baseUrl}}/getEnabledUserCount(initiativeId={{initiativeId3}})
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 7. ENABLED USER COUNT, missing initiativeId
# Expected: 400 Bad Request
### Get enabled user count — missing param, expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/getEnabledUserCount(initiativeId=null)
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# B. USAGE: TREND AND ROSTER (Screen 2 and Screen 3)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# 8. TREND COUNTS, WEEKLY, scoped to J4C
# Expected: 200 OK, 18 points, W23 to W40, activeCount:
#   2, 3, 4, 4, 5, 5, 5, 8, 8, 6, 7, 6, 6, 6, 10, 8, 8, 7
### Trend counts — WEEKLY, J4C
GET {{baseUrl}}/getTrendCounts(grain='WEEKLY',initiativeId={{initiativeId1}})
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 9. TREND COUNTS, MONTHLY, scoped to J4C
# Expected: 2026-06:5, 2026-07:8, 2026-08:10, 2026-09:11, 2026-10:5
### Trend counts — MONTHLY, J4C
GET {{baseUrl}}/getTrendCounts(grain='MONTHLY',initiativeId={{initiativeId1}})
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 10. TREND COUNTS, YEARLY, scoped to J4C
# Expected: 2026:12
### Trend counts — YEARLY, J4C
GET {{baseUrl}}/getTrendCounts(grain='YEARLY',initiativeId={{initiativeId1}})
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 11. TREND COUNTS, scoping check
# Expected: 2026-09 is 1 here (initiative 2), and 11 for J4C above. The unscoped
#           call in test 12 returns 12 for 2026-09, the sum of both.
### Trend counts — MONTHLY, initiative 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/getTrendCounts(grain='MONTHLY',initiativeId={{initiativeId2}})
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 12. TREND COUNTS, no initiativeId (all initiatives together)
# Expected: 2026-06:5, 07:8, 08:10, 09:12, 10:6
### Trend counts — MONTHLY, all initiatives
GET {{baseUrl}}/getTrendCounts(grain='MONTHLY')
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 13. TREND COUNTS, invalid grain
# Expected: 400 Bad Request, "Invalid grain: DAILY. Must be WEEKLY, MONTHLY, YEARLY."
### Trend counts — invalid grain, expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/getTrendCounts(grain='DAILY',initiativeId={{initiativeId1}})
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 14. ACTIVE USERS, all rows
# Expected: 200 OK. Each row has periodLabel, grain, person_scimId,
#           person_initiative_ID, firstSeen, lastSeen. No isEstimated field.
### Read all active user list entries
GET {{baseUrl}}/ActiveUsers
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 15. ACTIVE USERS, filter by grain
### Read active users filtered by MONTHLY grain
GET {{baseUrl}}/ActiveUsers?$filter=grain eq 'MONTHLY'
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 16. SCREEN 2 USER LIST: one period, scoped to J4C, person expanded
# Expected: 11 rows (J4C, MONTHLY, 2026-09), each with a person object.
# This is the path filter the Screen 2 controller uses. If it fails, use the
# foreign-key version in test 17.
### Active users for a period — path filter
GET {{baseUrl}}/ActiveUsers?$filter=grain eq 'MONTHLY' and periodLabel eq '2026-09' and person/initiative_ID eq {{initiativeId1}}&$expand=person
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 17. SAME QUERY with the foreign-key property
# Expected: the same 11 rows as test 16.
### Active users for a period — foreign-key filter
GET {{baseUrl}}/ActiveUsers?$filter=grain eq 'MONTHLY' and periodLabel eq '2026-09' and person_initiative_ID eq {{initiativeId1}}&$expand=person
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 18. SCREEN 2 ENABLED LIST
# Expected: 13 persons for J4C (11 active, 2 inactive)
### Persons of J4C
GET {{baseUrl}}/Persons?$filter=initiative_ID eq {{initiativeId1}}
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 19. SCREEN 3 PROFILE
# Expected: 1 row, scim-usr-0015, active true, initiativeName filled in
### One person's profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/Persons?$filter=scimId eq '{{scimId}}' and initiative_ID eq {{initiativeId1}}
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 20. SCREEN 3 ROSTER
# Expected: 4 rows for scim-usr-0015:
#   WEEKLY 2026-W39 (2026-09-22 to 2026-09-25), WEEKLY 2026-W40 (2026-09-28),
#   MONTHLY 2026-09 (2026-09-22 to 2026-09-28), YEARLY 2026 (2026-09-22 to 2026-09-28)
### One person's period rows
GET {{baseUrl}}/ActiveUsers?$filter=person_scimId eq '{{scimId}}' and person_initiative_ID eq {{initiativeId1}}
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# 21. NO CREDENTIALS
# Expected: 401 Unauthorized
### No credentials — expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/Initiatives


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# C. J4C USER SYNC (SCIM job, admin only). Skip these if you loaded the test CSVs.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### C1. Check current Person state
GET {{baseUrl}}/Persons
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}

### C2. Trigger the J4C user sync
# Expected: 200 OK, { created, reactivated, deactivated }
POST {{jobUrl}}/syncJ4CUsers
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### C3. Check Person state after the sync
GET {{baseUrl}}/Persons
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}

### C4. Run the sync again, it must be idempotent
# Expected: created:0, reactivated:0, deactivated:0
POST {{jobUrl}}/syncJ4CUsers
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### C5. Initiatives again, the enabledUsers count should match the active persons
GET {{baseUrl}}/Initiatives
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# D. J4C USAGE SYNC (audit log -> DailyAccess -> ActiveUserList -> cleanup)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### D1. Daily run: reads yesterday only (what the scheduled job sends)
# Expected: 200 OK, { scanned, accessEvents, matched, unmatchedUsers, rosterRows, cleaned }
# accessEvents is 0 if nobody signed in to Joule yesterday.
POST {{jobUrl}}/syncJ4CUsage
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### D2. Last 3 days including today (to see a sign-in you just made)
# Expected: 200 OK, same shape as D1
POST {{jobUrl}}/syncJ4CUsage
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "daysBack": 3 }

### D3. First run only: backfill the 90-day retention window
POST {{jobUrl}}/syncJ4CUsage
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "daysBack": 90 }

### D4. Run D1 twice in a row, it must be idempotent
# Expected: the second run gives the same matched count, and ActiveUsers has no new rows
POST {{jobUrl}}/syncJ4CUsage
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### D5. After a run, check the roster grew with real data
GET {{baseUrl}}/ActiveUsers?$filter=person_initiative_ID eq {{initiativeId1}}&$orderby=periodLabel desc&$top=20
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# E. ACCESS RULES AND MASKING
# Local mocked users (.cdsrc.json): admin needs the roles DashboardAdmin and
# DashboardUserDetail, viewer only DashboardViewer. In BTP the Admin role template
# already includes the other two scopes.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### E1. Viewer reads persons: names and emails are masked
# Expected: 200 OK, displayName like "J*** D***", email like "j***@example.com"
GET {{baseUrl}}/Persons?$top=3
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}

### E2. Admin reads persons: real values
# Expected: 200 OK, real names and emails (needs DashboardUserDetail on the admin user)
GET {{baseUrl}}/Persons?$top=3
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}

### E3. Viewer reads the roster with the person expanded: masked as well
# Expected: 200 OK, person.displayName and person.email masked
GET {{baseUrl}}/ActiveUsers?$top=3&$expand=person
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}

### E4. Viewer tries to start a job
# Expected: 403 Forbidden
POST {{jobUrl}}/syncJ4CUsage
Authorization: {{viewerAuth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### E5. No credentials on a job
# Expected: 401 Unauthorized
POST {{jobUrl}}/syncJ4CUsage
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### E6. The old reset endpoints are gone
# Expected: 404 Not Found
POST {{baseUrl}}/resetData
Authorization: {{adminAuth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}